    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Having to",
     "texto": [
      "To say that something is necessary or that you have to do it, use **-아/어야 해요** (I have to…, one must…).",
      "가다 → **가야 해요**, 먹다 → **먹어야 해요**, 쉬다 → **쉬어야 해요**, 하다 → **해야 해요**.",
      "약을 **먹어야 해요** = I have to take the medicine."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "How it is formed",
     "texto": [
      "The same vowel pattern as in -아/어요 is used: **-아야** after ㅏ/ㅗ and **-어야** in other cases; 하다 contracts to **해야**. Some irregular stems change, for example 듣다 → 들어야 해요. The final ㄹ is kept: 살다 → 살아야 해요, 만들다 → 만들어야 해요."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
